bug fixes for news
This is a belated reply to complaints about curdled .uindexes.:
The problem is usually due to running out of disk space.
The following is a new (untested) u_close() to go in index.c;
n_close() could be changed similarly.
(Alas, if this happens when rnews is running, the news will be lost
(nowhere to put it), and mail will probably be unable to report the loss.)

u_close()
{
	fclose(uindex);
	if (umode == UPDATE) {
		fflush(tuout);		/* Write out all of file */
		if (ferror(tuout)) {	/* Check for write error */
			unlink(TUFILE);
			xerror("write error on temporary .uindex file");
		}
		fclose(tuout);
		rename(TUFILE, UINDEX);
	}
}

In lieu of a shiny new version of news, here are a couple of easy hacks:
1. ".history" was theoretically motivated but is practically useless.
Delete the "else if (history..." code in input.c,
and the history() routine itself. Also the HISTORY variable.
And the .history file.  That should save some disk space.

2. In input.c, in uneti(), change "else insert(...);" to
"else { getdtln(); insert(...); }".
Otherwise, new news users will occasionally get inundated with old news.
